markdown <<MARKDOWN
# Cleaning Data

#### In this check for understanding level, students will practice **cleaning data** in Google Sheets.

<div style="background-color: #F5F7F8; color: #000000; padding: 15px; border-radius: 10px; width: 90%; margin: 20px auto;">
<p style = "font-size:14pt;"><strong>How to Clean Data:</strong></p>
  <ul style = "font-size:14pt;">
    <li>Fix errors such as misspelled words</li><br>
    <li>Create clearn categories such as "other"</li><br>
    <li>Delete unnecessary data such as "I don't know"</li>
</ul>
</div>

## 📝 To Do

#### Try out cleaning data in Google Sheets.

#### 1. Open the <a href="https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1MMsZwVwDaGNSol6RMsQk9NklsYBtgQyiEIxuSwmykIA/edit?usp=drive_link">Pizza Choice - Google Sheets</a>.
#### 2. For each response, decide if you want to:
- #### Keep it the same
- #### Delete it
- #### Change it

#### 3. Put your cleaned data in the second column--and graph it! See the sample below:

<br>

